(EASY STEPS TO MONEY MATTERS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MONEY is the medium by which we may acquire) Tj T*
(from others, who are willing to part with them,) Tj T*
(such things as we may desire.  The price of an) Tj T*
(article is the value set upon it by the possessor,) Tj T*
(as represented by an expressed sum in money.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The price of some things are arbitrarily fixed) Tj T*
(by law or custom, such as stamps, professional) Tj T*
(fees, duties, &c.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The standard of value in this country is gold,) Tj T*
(and it is as against gold, represented by coins) Tj T*
(of different denominations, that the value of all) Tj T*
(commodities is estimated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The authorised coins of the United Kingdom) Tj T*
(consist of the following pieces:-) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GOLD.) Tj T*
(    Five-sovereign piece, equal to Five pounds.) Tj T*
(    Two-sovereign piece, equal to Two pounds.) Tj T*
(    One-sovereign piece, equal to One pound.) Tj T*
(    Half-sovereign piece, equal to Half-a-pound.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SILVER.) Tj T*
(    A crown, or five-shilling piece, equal to one-) Tj T*
(fourth of a sovereign.) Tj T*
(    Double-fiorin, or four-shilling piece, equal to) Tj T*
(one-fifth of a sovereign.) Tj T*
(    Half-a-crown, or two shillings and sixpence,) Tj T*
(equal to one-eighth of a sovereign.) Tj T*
(    Florin, or two-shilling piece, equal to one-) Tj T*
(tenth of a sovereign.) Tj T*
(    Shilling piece, equal to one-twentieth of a) Tj T*
(sovereign.) Tj T*
