() Tj T*
(    AUTOMATIC RE-INVESTMENT OF DIVIDENDS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Holders of stock in the Funds who are not) Tj T*
(desirous of receiving their dividends, but prefer) Tj T*
(to have them added half-yearly to the capital) Tj T*
(sum without further action on their part, are) Tj T*
(granted facilities by which this may be done) Tj T*
(automatically, on application to the Bank of) Tj T*
(England.  The instructions apply to amounts of) Tj T*
(stock of less than г1,000 only.  These facilities) Tj T*
(are also extended to holders of Metropolitan) Tj T*
(Consolidated Stocks, and to the India 3 per) Tj T*
(cent. and 3 1/2 per cent. stocks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER VI.) Tj T*
(GOVERNMENT ANNUITIES.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE Commissioners for the Reduction of the) Tj T*
(National Debt, under the authority of Parlia-) Tj T*
(ment, grant annuities either on single lives, or) Tj T*
(on two lives and the life of the survivor, or on) Tj T*
(the joint continuance of two lives, such annui-) Tj T*
(ties to commence immediately.  In the case of) Tj T*
(single lives, the annuity _may_ be made to com-) Tj T*
(mence at a future period, and the consideration) Tj T*
(for it may be paid by the purchaser annually in) Tj T*
(sums of money not less than г5, but in case of) Tj T*
(default in keeping up the annual instalments,) Tj T*
(all the annual payments previously made are) Tj T*
(forfeited, and all right to the annuity is ex-) Tj T*
(tinguished.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Payment for an annuity is made by the) Tj T*
(transfer of 2 1/2 per cent. Consols, or money of equi-) Tj T*
(valent value, at the price of the stock on the day) Tj T*
(of the transaction.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The tables \(see p.44\) show the annuity which) Tj T*
(г100 of 2 1/2 per cent. stock will purchase, to con-) Tj T*
(tinue during the life of a nominee at the re-) Tj T*
(spective ages and according to the prices of 2 1/2) Tj T*
(per cent. stock therein stated.  It will be seen) Tj T*
(that in the case of money being paid for the) Tj T*
(purchase of the annuity, the higher the price of) Tj T*
(Consols the dearer will be the purchase.  Thus,) Tj T*
(a female buying an annuity at the age of fifty,) Tj T*
(amounting to г5 19s. 8d. per annum, and Consols) Tj T*
(being at _par_, or 100, would, if she paid for it) Tj T*
