(They consist of loans raised in this country for) Tj T*
(the use of the Indian Government and are two) Tj T*
(in number, bearing interest respectively at the) Tj T*
(rate of 3 and 3 1/2 per cent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    There is also what is termed a Rupee Paper) Tj T*
(Loan, raised in India at 3 1/2 per cent. per annum.) Tj T*
(The interest is paid in the currency of the coun-) Tj T*
(try, which is the rupee, and that coin being) Tj T*
(worth only a little more than half its nominal) Tj T*
(value in this country, the investor in this stock) Tj T*
(would receive in the shape of interest little more) Tj T*
(than half the г3 10s. a year.  The price of the) Tj T*
(stock in the market is consequently in the same) Tj T*
(proportion, and at the present moment is about) Tj T*
(г62 for every г100 stock.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHAPTER VII.) Tj T*
(LOANS TO CORPORATIONS AND COUNTIES OF) Tj T*
(THE UNITED KINGDOM.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THESE are loans raised by boroughs and coun-) Tj T*
(ties, and other authorities in this country, for) Tj T*
(local purposes, upon the security of the rates or) Tj T*
(other assured income.  Before the money is) Tj T*
(borrowed the consent of the Local Government) Tj T*
(Board is necessary to make the loan legal, and) Tj T*
(evidence is required that the resources of the) Tj T*
(borrowers are ample to meet their obligations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    On most of these stocks the rate of interest is) Tj T*
(3 per cent., though there are some few at 3 1/2 per) Tj T*
(cent.  The principal is redeemable at fixed dates,) Tj T*
(or by a sinking fund, that is, by setting aside so) Tj T*
(much a year to pay off the loan at a fixed time,) Tj T*
(or as opportunity offers.  For instance, in times) Tj T*
(when money is scarce or dear there is a proba-) Tj T*
(bility of these stocks falling below their par) Tj T*
(value, and the Sinking Fund is then used to buy) Tj T*
(the stock in the market.  Thus the Corporation) Tj T*
(may be able in effect to pay off a loan of г100) Tj T*
(for г90 or г95, whatever the price may be, and) Tj T*
(so gain the amount of the difference.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Investments in securities of this kind may be) Tj T*
(considered absolutely safe, although certainly) Tj T*
(there is the contingent risk of a town, after bor-) Tj T*
(rowing up to its full powers, drifting into decay) Tj T*
(from the loss of its staple trade, and so finding) Tj T*
(itself unable to meet its obligations.  The in-) Tj T*
