(THE main object of a Building Society is to aid) Tj T*
(a man to become proprietor of his own dwelling.) Tj T*
(This can be accomplished by means of the society) Tj T*
(in two different ways:- 1, by depositing with) Tj T*
(the society periodical money savings until, with) Tj T*
(the interest allowed, enough has been accumu-) Tj T*
(lated to buy a house; 2, by borrowing from the) Tj T*
(society a sufficient sum to purchase a house) Tj T*
(and repaying the loan, with interest, by instal-) Tj T*
(ments spread over a term of years.  A person) Tj T*
(desiring to become a depositor must qualify for) Tj T*
(membership of the society by paying an entrance) Tj T*
(fee of; say, 2s. 6d.  He then takes up a share and,) Tj T*
(by paying periodical instalments according to) Tj T*
(the tables, he becomes entitled at the end of the) Tj T*
(appointed time to receive г100.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
