(CHAPTER XI.) Tj T*
(THE POST OFFICE SAVINGS BANK.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THIS institution offers a most admirable, con-) Tj T*
(venient, and secure depository for the savings of) Tj T*
(the industrial classes and of others.  Its value) Tj T*
(to the thrifty and timid investor is incalculable,) Tj T*
(for here he may rest satisfied that he has abso-) Tj T*
(lute security, and the system is so hedged about) Tj T*
(with safeguards that it is difficult to discover) Tj T*
(any means by which loss can be sustained.  The) Tj T*
(interest allowed is not high, but reasonable) Tj T*
(enough when the perfect security and the facili-) Tj T*
(ties offered are taken into consideration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Money may be deposited by any person over) Tj T*
(seven years of age, and by anyone on behalf of) Tj T*
(children under seven.  Also by married women,) Tj T*
(and with this advantage, that such deposits,) Tj T*
(unless and until the contrary is proved, are) Tj T*
(deemed to be the property of such married) Tj T*
(woman; moreover, the fact that any deposit is) Tj T*
(standing in the name of a married woman) Tj T*
(being _prima facie_ evidence that she is entitled) Tj T*
(to draw the same without the consent of her) Tj T*
(husband.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Deposits may be made by two or more per-) Tj T*
(sons, provided no one of them has any other) Tj T*
(account in a Savings Bank, and by one person) Tj T*
(as trustee for another person.  On opening an) Tj T*
(account a person has to sign a declaration to the) Tj T*
(effect that he takes no personal benefit from any) Tj T*
(other account in the Post Office Savings Bank) Tj T*
(or in a Trustee Savings Bank, and should this) Tj T*
(declaration not be true all sums so deposited) Tj T*
(will be liable to forfeiture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    Any person opening an account, that is, de-) Tj T*
(positing money with a Post Office Savings Bank,) Tj T*
(will receive a book in which the amount is) Tj T*
(entered, and the signature of the Postmaster and) Tj T*
(stamp of the office affixed to the entry.  In) Tj T*
(addition to this he will receive from the depart-) Tj T*
(ment in London, a few days after, a receipt for) Tj T*
(the amount.  Once in each year, on the anni-) Tj T*
(versary of the day on which his first deposit was) Tj T*
(made, the depositor should forward his book to) Tj T*
(the Controller of Savings Banks, London, in) Tj T*
(order that it may be compared with the books) Tj T*
(of the department in London, and that the in-) Tj T*
